nina: Quick question for docs folks. There's a broken crosslink from /dedicated/faq.md to the provisioning guide (anchor mismatch). Also want to add an SDK snippet showing how to set `isolation_level` to `strict`.

chris: I'll fix the crosslink and add the Python + JS snippet. For the JS snippet I'm going to show how the SDK handles preemption callbacks.

oliver: I'll handle updating the FAQ and SLA table. Noting that support keeps getting questions about preemption vs eviction; we should standardize language to preemption across Dedicated docs.

docs-bot: link-checker: dedicated/faq.md -> broken anchor at line 12: `#capacity-preempt` (typo). Suggestion: `#capacity-preemption`.

nina: Thanks. Let's ensure the migration note covers `max_batches` -> `max_concurrent_batches` and `burst_limit` -> `burst_capacity`. Also tag security for docs on the private deployment interaction with isolation settings.

chris: Draft JS snippet:
```js
client.dedicated.on('preemption', (evt) => {
  // evt.models contains fallback mapping
  console.log('preempted, switching to fallback model', evt.models);
});

await client.dedicated.updateScalePolicy('policy-id', {
  isolation_level: 'strict',
});
```

oliver: I'll reword SLA table row to make clear that burst is best-effort and not covered by the committed uptime SLA. 

nina: Great. I'll open a tiny PR for the anchor fix so the rest of the work isn't blocked.

chris: PRs: anchor fix https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/458, JS snippets https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/459.

oliver: I'll add inline edits to the SLA doc after snippets land.

docs-bot: preview build: all checks pass for anchor fix PR.

nina: Thanks team. We'll mark migration guide with `migration: yes` frontmatter.
